{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Etelä-Pohjanmaa's crude symptomatic treatment share is 28.1% (95% CI 24.5–32.1; n=152/540), where the 95% confidence interval excludes the national 39.5% (5871/14873) and lies below it.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:symptomatic:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:symptomatic"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories where a patient can have several treatments, the crude curative share is 30.6% (95% CI 26.8–34.6; n=165/540), whose 95% confidence interval includes the national 27.0% (4009/14873), while the crude life-prolonging share is 40.4% (95% CI 36.3–44.6; n=218/540), whose 95% confidence interval excludes the national 30.4% (4522/14873) and lies above it.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "For the crude share with no treatment record within 12 months, Etelä-Pohjanmaa is at 25.7% (95% CI 22.2–29.6; n=139/540), whose 95% confidence interval includes the national 27.5% (4089/14873), and this category mixes untreated patients and unrecorded treatment.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Etelä-Pohjanmaa's crude share with an MDT meeting recorded is 32.4% (95% CI 28.6–36.5; n=175/540), whose 95% confidence interval excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873) and lies above it, though HILMO procedure codes are entered only from direct patient contacts and therefore measure recording practice rather than care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "While public data do not measure county wait times from symptoms, referrals, or treatment start, preliminary, unpublished national averages show 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland versus 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark, comprising 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "County treatment shares in Taulukko 11 are crude: they lack age adjustment and separately cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of patients.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "q:7885b0974f"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "In the 2019–2023 report, county-level age-adjusted treatment shares appear only in Kuva 16 (a PNG figure, by sex, with 95% CIs), where the digitised national age-adjusted curative reference lines are 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women (±0.5 percentage points), whereas Taulukko 11 gives only crude county shares.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A journal article found that hospital discharge register (HILMO) diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types, which concerns diagnosis concordance only and not treatment, referral, or MDT recording, while overall lung cancer data reporting, collection, and storage remain incomplete and Finland has no cancer quality registry.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:47c7e11303",
          "filha:registry"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public report data do not measure symptom onset or referral dates, outpatient primary care visits are not included in the report's data, occupational health is not mentioned at all, and imaging appears only indirectly as diagnosis based on clinical examination alone, such as imaging, in approximately 20% of patients without imaging waits.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The report tracks whether a specialist visit occurs within 12 months (93.6% nationally) and treatment type within 12 months, but not county visit or treatment start dates, while mentor insight indicates that a weak referral gets a lower urgency rating in specialist care and occupational health gets patients to specialist care faster.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "mentor:hanna_occupational"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends reporting THL 21/2016 access times with handover alerts, standardising referrals with a diagnostic-phase contact, and publishing per-county coding coverage for stage, drug treatment, and MDT meetings.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "q:24169121a4",
        "q:556431a0c2",
        "q:950a2f797b"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion and national access-time monitoring is lacking, the team recommends reporting access times using THL guidance 21/2016 definitions (for 16 cancers) with handover alerts, while the STM roadmap (measure 3.1.2) plans national pathway descriptions and access times by 2026–2028 and 2029–2031.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:4e702a20fe",
          "q:ccda20dce9",
          "q:ed87906241",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:b326e35410"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Since referrals follow local instructions and mentor insight notes weak referrals get lower urgency ratings, the team recommends a standard referral template, a persistent-symptoms referral rule after a normal X-ray, and a diagnostic-phase contact, while the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation with primary-care referral criteria and recommended time limits is to be carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:29b792498e",
          "q:8c9c032c25",
          "q:614febebf2",
          "q:14dff3e002"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "To support the team's recommendation for standardised referrals and a named diagnostic-phase contact before national models take effect, the STM roadmap plans standardised referral criteria and symptom-based models in national pathways (measure 2.5.2) by 2026–2028 and 2029–2031, and plans care-coordinator guidance (measure 1.2.3) by 2026–2028 for county adoption by 2029–2031 while mapping which care phase to target.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:0780bf74b0",
          "q:37bb4c3b38",
          "q:9a1cd194f5",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:e31448e9c9",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because stage is missing for about 48% of patients nationally and MDT codes capture only direct patient contacts—with Etelä-Pohjanmaa's crude MDT-recorded share at 32.4% (95% CI 28.6–36.5; n=175/540) versus 6.0% (893/14873) nationally—the team recommends publishing per-county stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding coverage while the STM roadmap (measure 3.2.1) plans a quality registry decree update by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "q:f07a34a300"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
